+# Trace of one raw event through Mycelic: findings
+
+Engineer-A (trace/audit), overnight repair 2026-10-09. Model that ran this audit: `claude-sonnet-5-5` (from the session's own system prompt).
+
+Everything below comes from `python research/mycelic_e2e/audit/trace_one_event.py` (about 40 s, writes `trace_output.json` next to it)
+or from the existing tests named in "Baseline". Ids in the table are from the saved `trace_output.json`; a re-run produces new ids
+(the structure, counts and verdicts repeat across runs once the harness fixes listed at the end were in; the script was run several times while it was being written).
+
+## What was run, and what was not
+
+| item | value |
+|---|---|
+| code | branch `claude/mycelic-implementation-vr034p` content at `f96f263` plus uncommitted edits other engineers were making in the same working copy while this ran (at 05:52 UTC `git diff --stat`: `mycelic/knowledge/gate.py` and `support.py`, 76 insertions and 10 deletions; untracked `mycelic/knowledge/units.py` and `mycelic/db/migrations/0005_hypergraph.sql`). Nothing in `mycelic/` was modified by this audit, and the probe outcomes below did not change across runs made while those edits landed. |
+| composition | `build_runtime(settings)` + `create_app(rt, ..., run_worker=True, run_holders=True)`: coord.db, org/authz, durable job queue, `LoopEngine`, SQLite-outbox transport, `DefaultModelRouter` over the deterministic `FakeProvider`, hash embeddings, embedded holders (one NeuralGraph store per holder with `IngestRuntime`). The discovery worker runs inside the API process, exactly as `MYCELIC_RUN_WORKER_IN_API=1` does. |
+| entry points | HTTP only (aiohttp test server on the real routes): register tenant, units, invitations, `POST /api/holders`, `POST /api/holders/{id}/connectors`, `PATCH .../sources`, `POST .../sync`, `POST .../webhook` + the public signed webhook, `POST /api/goals`, `POST /api/questions`, reads of goals/discoveries/claims/evidence. The only non-HTTP actions: writing the export file into the holder's `imports/` directory (what `routes_integrations.upload_import` does for the UI), and `HolderService.heartbeat_once()` (the call the holder's 20 s heartbeat loop makes) so the registry row is current. |
+| connector | `local_export`, `source_app="slack-export"` (a label; this is a Slack-style export, not the Slack connector). The Slack/GitHub/Gmail/Drive mock connectors were not driven. |
+| tenant | "Acme Freight Group": region Europe; departments Logistics (teams Ocean Freight, Port Operations), Sales (Key Accounts), Finance (Treasury); users lena (regional lead, owns the goal), ana, bo, cy, dee (employees, one holder each); owner-declared holder domains `operations.logistics` (ana, bo, cy) and `finance` (dee). |
+| not tested | NATS, separate holder processes, a real model provider (so every "the model said X" below is the fake's lexical rule), sharded holders, the UI. |
+
+Baseline: `python -m pytest mycelic/tests/test_loop_engine.py mycelic/tests/test_ingest_events.py mycelic/tests/test_ingest_pipeline.py mycelic/tests/test_integrations_api.py -q` was run once at about 05:49 UTC against the then working tree: **41 passed**.
+
+The event, as written to the export file (variant A, literal; `ts` 1790674800.000100):
+`{"type":"message","id":"1790674800.000100","event_id":"Ev0ROTTERDAM9D","author":"U0ANA","created_at":"2026-10-08T09:12:00+00:00","text":"Acme Freight shipment into Rotterdam slipped another 9 days","container_name":"#ocean-freight"}`,
+channel `C0OCEAN` "#ocean-freight" (public), account `T0ACME`. Variant B is the same message with the words
+"Recurring blocker: ... customs paperwork caused the delay." added, because the fake rules key on such words (see "first loss point").
+
