+
+## Probes
+
+Verdict scale: PASS (expected behaviour observed), FAIL (expected behaviour absent), DEFECT (behaviour observed that a reviewer would call wrong), LIMITATION (undetectable by design).
+Observed values are from `trace_output.json` under `probes.*`.
+
+### a. Duplicate delivery of the same provider event: **PASS**
+One message delivered by: first sync; second sync of the unchanged file; the identical JSON line appended and synced; a signed push notice (`POST /api/webhooks/local_export/{endpoint}`) twice with the same `delivery_id`; then a push notice with a new `delivery_id`.
+- sync 2: `raw_items 0` (cursor passed the line). Appended duplicate: `raw_items 1, duplicates 1, enqueued 0`. Push d1: http 200 `routed 1`; redelivered d1: `routed 0` (webhook_deliveries dedupe); push d2: `routed 1`, fetched and recognised.
+- Final holder counts: `ingest_records 1, ingest_versions 1, documents 1, memories 1, applied_events 1`, queue `done/new 1`, outbox 1. Coordinator: `document.ingested` 1, transport messages 7 with 7 distinct msg_ids.
+- The pipeline's stage metrics show the duplicates were evaluated (`fetch/ok` 8, `dedupe/new` 1), i.e. recognised and dropped, not lost.
+
+### b. Replay after restart (close + reopen coordinator and holders on the same dirs): **PASS**
+Variant-B event ingested, goal run to idle (1 claim, 1 discovery, 1 evidence ref, 3 questions, 6 responses, 17 transport messages), then `Runtime.stop()` (worker, holders to offline, transport, db closed) and `build_runtime` on the same data dir.
+- After reopen and again after a re-sync of the unchanged file plus `POST /goals/{id}/loop run_now`: holder counts identical (ignoring metric counters), coordinator counts identical (17 transport messages, 17 distinct, 1 claim, 1 discovery, 3 questions, 6 responses), claims identical, re-sync `raw_items 0`, goal back to `waiting` ("nothing useful to ask right now"), the holder still finds the memory by search (1 hit). Jobs: 13 done, 0 dead.
+
+### c. Out-of-order edits (older `updated_at` delivered after newer): **PASS** on ordering; see c2 for the coordinator side
+Original T0 09:12 ("9 days"); edit T2 11:00 ("12 days") synced; then edit T1 10:00 ("3 days") appended and synced.
+- Queue outcomes in order: `new`, `update`, `historical`. After T2: document `revised` v2 with the 12-day text, memory 1 `superseded` + 1 active. After the late T1: document unchanged (still 12 days, `current_version 2026-10-08T11:00:00`), memories 1 active / 2 total, `ingest_versions` gains a `...#historical` row with `doc_version null`; no text of the 3-day edit exists in the holder DB (needle `slipped 3 days`: 0 hits).
+
+### c2. An author's own edit makes the earlier claim "contested": **DEFECT** (design-level; judgement call)
+Same setup. After the T2 edit the loop re-verified the claim (verification question trigger `evidence_revised`, answered by the *same* holder), then opened a contradiction follow-up. Observed: claim A (9 days) `contested` v4, claim B (12 days) `contested` v2, one conflict `investigating` "verification disagrees: ... 12 days ...", old ref `revised`, two new active refs with the new root. One person editing one message produced a conflict between the old and new version of that message; nothing marks claim A as superseded by B. Also note the root changes on edit (`root_110e...` -> `root_ca7b...`, by design per INGESTION.md 4.5).
+
+### d. Edit then delete: **DEFECT**
+After the edits, a `delete` line (T3 12:00) was synced, then an `edit` older than the delete (11:30) arrived late.
+- Holder: record `deletion_status purged`, document `deleted` with empty text, memories `retracted` with empty text, 0 live records, entities 0; needles `customs paperwork`, `12 days`, `9 days` have 0 hits in the holder DB (FTS tables included). The only hit for the event is `ingest_versions.source_event_id = Ev0ROTTERDAM9D` (an identifier, and my own event id contains the string). The late older edit: `excluded 1`, no resurrection (`live_records 0`, `memories_active 0`).
+- Coordinator: 3 evidence refs `retracted` with empty excerpt; both claims `retracted`, text `[removed: source deleted]`. **But verbatim event text survives in** `questions.result`, `question_runs.state`, `conflicts.summary`, `conflicts.investigation`, `jobs.result`, `events.payload` and `transport_messages.payload` (needle `customs paperwork` found in all seven, carrying the 9-day and/or the 12-day wording). The deletion withdrew the structured copies and left the derived/log copies.
+
+### e. Malformed event and missing metadata: **DEFECT** (explicit count, no identification)
+9 data lines: a good record; unparsable JSON; a JSON array; a message without `id`; a message with no author and no timestamps; a message without text; unknown type `telepathy`; a message with timestamps `"yesterday-ish"`/`"soon"`; a message with `text: null`.
+- Sync response: `raw_items 9, enqueued 3, normalize_errors 6`. Records created: `m-good`, `m-nometa`, `m-badts`. Stage metrics: `normalize/error 6, normalize/ok 3`. 9 = 3 + 6, so nothing vanished unaccounted.
+- But which six lines were rejected and why exists nowhere: holder `audit_log` has only the 3 `document.ingest` rows, coordinator `audit_log` has only `connector.install`/`connector.sources`, connector health is `{}` / status `active`, the dead-letter list is `[]`, and a second sync reports `raw_items 0, normalize_errors 0` (the cursor moved past them). The rejected content is "not kept anywhere" (`pipeline.py:_prepare_page` comment) and logged at INFO with an error code only.
+- Missing metadata is accepted silently: `m-nometa` (no author, no timestamps) is stored with `created_at_src null`, `author_entity_id null`, and its document `observed_at` is the **ingest time of that run** rather than null; `m-badts` likewise (`m-good` keeps its own 2026-10-08T09:12:00Z). Evidence freshness is "as fresh as observed_at", so an undated old message looks fresh.
+
+### f. Common origin (same original text forwarded by 3 users in 3 teams): **DEFECT** (verbatim forwards PASS; explicit lineage without text overlap FAIL)
+Each variant: ana, bo, cy (Ocean Freight, Port Operations, Key Accounts) each ingest their own message; goal run; claim support read.
+
+| variant | roots (holder-side `root_method`) | claim support |
+|---|---|---|
+| f1 `forwarded_from` metadata + verbatim body | 1 distinct root, `content` | hypothesis, `independent_roots 1`, `copied_refs 2` (PASS) |
+| f2 text `---------- Forwarded message ---------` block + own note | 1 distinct root, `pure_copy` | hypothesis, `independent_roots 1`, `copied_refs 2` (PASS) |
+| f3 verbatim copy, no marker | 1 distinct root, `content` | hypothesis, `independent_roots 1`, `copied_refs 2` (PASS) |
+| f1b `forwarded_from` naming the same origin, but each person's own words | **3** distinct roots, `content` | **supported, `independent_roots 3`, `copied_refs 0`** (DEFECT) |
+| f4 retold in own words, no marker | 3 distinct roots | supported, `independent_roots 3` (LIMITATION: undetectable) |
+
+Why f1b fails: `events.py:compute_root` uses `derived_from` only if the named original is "a known local record" (`resolve_explicit`); here it is not held by any of the three, so the root falls back to the person's own text. `derived_from` is then **not persisted** (the origin object id `1790674800.000100` has 0 hits in each holder DB) and never reaches the coordinator, so three people who all declared "this is a forward of X" count as three independent roots and a claim becomes `supported`. It follows INGESTION.md 4.5, so it is a spec gap rather than a coding slip.
+
+### g. Three observations of one entity, 3 holders in 2 departments: **PASS** (with two gaps)
+ana (Logistics/Ocean Freight), bo (Logistics/Port Operations), cy (Sales/Key Accounts), each a different message (author, channel, timestamp, wording) about Acme Freight + Rotterdam + "9 days".
+- The gap question (`operations.logistics`) was routed to **all three** and answered by all three; the claim "Customer Acme Freight escalated a recurring blocker: the Rotterdam delivery slipped 9 days..." has `independent_roots 3`, `copied_refs 0`, three distinct `root_*` ids, status **supported**; gate audit: "3 independent source roots (policy needs 2)"; discovery kind `finding`, level region.
+- Gap 1: routing worked only because the owners declared `operations.logistics`. **g2:** with the same three holders and the same content but no declared domains, no question was routed at all (0 questions, 0 routes); holder registry `domains []`, `published_domains []` (one record per holder is below the 5-record publication threshold). The goal sat in `waiting` with the explanation "no new question could be formed (duplicates or cooldown)", which is not the cause (there were no candidate domains).
+- Gap 2: no shared entity exists to link them: each holder's `entities` are only `slack-export message`, a domain node and the person node. The three records were classified `operations`, `unclassified` and `operations.logistics`.
+
+### h. Denied access (dee: Treasury team, Finance department, no membership under Logistics or Sales): **PASS** for content; one metadata DEFECT (h2)
+As dee: goal 403; discovery list `[]`; claim list `[]`; discovery/claim/evidence by id 403; another user's holder `search`/`records`/`documents` 403; `POST /api/questions` scoped to Logistics 403; unit agent chat for Logistics 403; personal agent chat answers "I have no authorized knowledge that answers that." (0 claims, 0 discoveries, 0 memories in context); `/me/memory/search` 0 results. No needle (`Rotterdam`, `Acme Freight`, `9 days`, `customs`) appears in any response body once the caller's own echoed query text is removed. A question dee was allowed to create from dee's own unit ended `failed / no_authorized_holders` and routed to none of the Logistics holders. Positive controls: lena (regional lead) sees the goal, discovery, claim, evidence; bo (Logistics employee, other team) gets 403 on the same objects.
+- Restricted source: a channel with `visibility members` and members {ana, bo} produced 4 `no_evidence` responses (`memory_count 0`), 0 claims, and no event text in coord.db; the same channel with members {ana, lena, admin} (the whole answer audience) produced an answered response and 1 claim. The audience filter is applied before retrieval and is not simply blocking everything.
+- **h2 (DEFECT, minor):** dee can read their own failed question, whose `result.rejected` lists the opaque ids of the three Logistics holders with reason "holder owner is outside the question's scope" and the fourth with "no matching evidence domain". No content, but a refused asker learns that three holders exist elsewhere and which of them match the domain.
+
+### i. Cross-tenant: **PASS**
+A second tenant "Globex" in the same coordinator and holder host. Using Acme ids, Globex's lead and admin got 404 on the goal, discovery, claim, evidence (and `/raw`), the holder's `search` and `records`, the Acme unit, 404 on `POST /api/questions` with an Acme unit or goal, 404 on adding a membership to an Acme unit, 403 on creating a goal owned by an Acme unit; `GET /api/discoveries` returned 0 items. A Globex goal with the same domain (`operations.logistics`) and two Globex holders routed only to Globex holders (0 routes to non-Globex holders; 0 Acme routes to Globex holders), got 2 `no_evidence`, 0 claims, and no Acme needle in its goal detail.
+
+## First loss point
+
+**Literal event (variant A): stage 6, the holder's answer step, on the loop's own question.** The event is intact and traceable through every stage before it (stages 1-5, 9: canonical record, root, queue disposition `new`, domain, single shard, memory, outbox, coordinator `document.ingested`). When the discovery loop asks, ana's holder retrieves the memory (`memory_count 1`) and the `answer_from_evidence` task returns `no_evidence`, because the loop's question is the fixed template `What recurring operational blockers related to operations.logistics have you recorded, and what caused them?` (`models/fake.py:draft_question`, `fake_rules` in `models/tasks.py`), which shares 0 content tokens with "Acme Freight shipment into Rotterdam slipped another 9 days" (the fake rule needs 2). The goal's words (Rotterdam, Acme Freight) are in the gap description and in the `draft_question` input, but the template drops them. Result: 4 `no_evidence` responses, 0 claims, 0 discoveries, both questions `retained_uncertain`.
+
+Two qualifications that matter for how far this generalises:
+1. The loss is produced by the deterministic fake provider's rules. The real `draft_question` task is given `goal` and `gap` (`discovery/engine.py:_ask_for_gap`), so a real model could write a question that names Rotterdam; this audit cannot tell whether it would. What the run does show regardless of the rule details: the A goal ended in state `waiting` with exactly two questions (one per candidate domain) and nothing further, i.e. one `no_evidence` round per domain closed the coverage question. From reading `LoopEngine.tick` (not from a run): `uncovered = [d for d in domains if d not in covered and d not in attempted]`, and `attempted` is every domain that already had a depth-0 gap question, whatever its outcome, so the loop does not re-ask a domain with different wording. Candidate domains come only from owner-declared holder domains or domains published at >= 5 records (g2).
+2. Once a question carries the event's words, the event is not lost: step 8 shows the literal event answered, committed as a claim with the full chain, and a discovery of kind **hypothesis** (`independent_roots 1`, the gate needs 2). It reaches a committed discovery only as a hypothesis; it can become `supported` only with independent support from other roots (probe g: 3 roots -> supported).
+
+**Variant B (event with words the fake rules match)** reaches a committed discovery without a loss: `ev_365745cce25ebc9a99c1` -> `claim_2f233c62e5e54204ab2f` (hypothesis) -> `disc_b21e11f5a313403cae9c` (hypothesis), provenance chain verified to `rec_e39007e2aa31989a58a0630a` / source object `1790674800.000100`.
+
+## Other defects found along the way
+
+1. Rejected input is counted but not identified (e). 2. Deletion leaves verbatim copies in 7 coordinator tables (d). 3. `forwarded_from` lineage is dropped and cannot unify roots across holders (f1b). 4. An edit contests the claim derived from its own earlier version (c2). 5. A holder with relevant content but no declared domains and < 5 records is invisible to the loop, and the loop's explanation says "duplicates or cooldown" (g2). 6. Missing timestamps become ingest-time freshness (e). 7. Opaque holder ids and rejection reasons are visible to a refused asker (h2). 8. Entity extraction is off in the production composition (stage 4).
+
+## Harness notes (so the verdicts can be trusted)
+
+Fixed while writing, none changes a product result: a needle check that counted the caller's own echoed query (`/me/memory/search`, the question text returned to its asker) as a leak; a Globex goal whose own title named Rotterdam; a state comparison that included metric counters that legitimately move on restart; the event id `Ev0ROTTERDAM9D` containing the needle `Rotterdam`. Probes are each run in a fresh temp data dir (`tempfile.mkdtemp`), removed at exit; `/home/user/NeuralGraph` is never touched.
